1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The ancient Chinese saw — a
vermilion bird.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:11,000
China’s sky has four great beasts. The
last of them: the Vermilion Bird of the
south.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Seven lunar mansions form one bird. Sima
Qian: Liu the beak, Xing the neck, Zhang
the crop, Yi the wings.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Its other name is Chun, “quail”. Its
middle third: Chunhuo, “Quail Fire”.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
But the bird that laid it wasn’t the
Vermilion Bird.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The Shang watched another star: the
Great Fire, the Azure Dragon’s heart.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The Guoyu says Jupiter stood in Quail
Fire that year — Zhou’s own field of
sky.

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Jupiter is back in Quail Fire. Look east
after dark: it’s the brightest light.

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Next, on 17 Feb: the Sámi reindeer hunt.

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

